# Build context for the Glama introspection image (`Dockerfile`).
#
# The install step is `pip install --no-deps .` from this directory, so the
# context has to keep exactly what `pyproject.toml` reads: the package sources,
# README.md (`readme =`) and LICENSE (`license-files =`). Everything else listed
# here is weight the image never looks at - a checkpoint alone would be ~650 MB
# of build context.

# Version control and CI
.git
.github

# Caches and build output
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Tests are not part of the installed package and nothing in it imports them.
tests/

# Model weights and local scratch, none of which this image loads.
_models/
_wheels/
_upstream-src/
*.safetensors
*.bin
calibration.json

# Documentation, except the one file the packaging metadata requires. Order
# matters: the negation has to come after the pattern it re-includes, or the
# image builds with a README the metadata points at and the wheel build fails.
*.md
!README.md

# `src/laya_mcp/SKILL.md` is not documentation. It is declared in
# `[tool.setuptools.package-data]` and vendored inside the package so an installed
# wheel can read it, which makes it a build input rather than a document.
# Re-included explicitly even though `*.md` is meant to hit the repository-root
# documents only: the cost of being wrong is a wheel that ships without its
# package data, and a negation that matches nothing costs nothing.
!src/laya_mcp/SKILL.md
